WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.401
Tonight, breaking news.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.103
Federal prosecutors have notified former

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:03.770
President Trump

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.104
that he is

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:04.804
now the target

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.406
of a criminal investigation in the Mar

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.874
a Lago documents case.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:08.508
This is federal

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.576
prosecutors are wrapping up

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.710
their investigation

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.479
and a potential indictment

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.980
could come really at any time.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.614
At this point,

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.482
we're also learning

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.616
that the DOJ is planning

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.018
on bringing a significant portion

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.652
of any charges in the case.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.121
At a federal court in South Florida.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:21.454
Now, that's

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.622
according to The Washington Post.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.356
We're going to talk about more

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.958
about what that means in a moment.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.593
I want to begin with Paula Reid OUTFRONT

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.660
with so much of this reporting.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.995
What are you learning, Paula?

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:29.329
Well, Erin,

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.063
we've learned that former

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.798
President Trump has been informed

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.066
that he is the target

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.501
of a federal investigation

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.301
into the possible

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.604
mishandling of classified documents.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.372
Now, this is a sign

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.874
that prosecutors could be moving

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.108
closer to possibly

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.344
indicting the former president.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.812
We are told that his legal team

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.479
was informed

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.281
via a target letter that he is

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.350
now the focus of this investigation.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.118
Multiple sources have learned

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.752
about the letter

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.120
having it described to them,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.588
though none of our sources

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.389
have directly

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.458
or personally seen this letter.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.759
But really, crystallizes

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.094
the fact that the special counsel,

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:01.928
Jack Smith, in

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.763
this investigation is focused

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.231
on former President Trump

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.667
and not just the people around him.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:08.701
Usually,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.836
if you are the recipient

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:10.670
of a target letter,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.405
it means that you have the opportunity

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.373
if you would like

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.575
to go before a grand jury.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.342
Now, it's unclear

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.143
if the former president

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:17.844
would do that, though

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.045
it does seem unlikely

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.680
that his legal team would advise that.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.748
It's also something

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.449
that he was offered up

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.083
in Manhattan

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.951
in the recent civil case and opted

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.286
not to do that.

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.587
Now, we know his attorneys met

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.189
with the Justice Department earlier

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:29.956
this week

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.690
to discuss

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.758
what they believe

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.893
are problems with this case.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.828
And as we know, former

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.796
President Trump has repeatedly said

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.298
that he has done nothing wrong.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.065
So you're also getting

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:39.966
some breaking details,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.968
I know, Paula, about Steve Bannon

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.269
and the other investigation

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.071
about January six. What's that?

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:45.505
That's right.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.272
And the special counsel's

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.475
other investigation into January six.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.043
We've learned that former White House

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.044
adviser and longtime

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:51.711
Trump ally

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.880
Steve Bannon has been subpoenaed

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.748
to testify, though it's unclear

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.418
how cooperative a witness he will be.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:58.885
Of course,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.019
he was recently convicted

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.988
for being in contempt of Congress.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.356
He's facing a potential prison

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.157
sentence there.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:04.691
So it's unclear

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.558
if he's going to play ball.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.226
It's a little different

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.727
with the federal investigation

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.828
but he also has the opportunity,

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.164
if he so chooses, to plead the Fifth.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.031
But this is, of course,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.200
a significant witness for them to call.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.468
We've learned in terms

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.237
of a more cooperative witness

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.238
our colleague Zach Cohen

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.639
and I broke the story today

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.573
that those investigators

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.142
in the January six investigation

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:25.111
also recently spoke with Alyssa Farah

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:25.812
Griffith.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.847
She is, of course, a top communications

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.516
advisor in the Trump White House.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.417
She was brought on by Mark Meadows.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.252
And it's interesting,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.520
she just had an interview

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.187
with investigators.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.622
She didn't go before the grand jury.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.390
But one of the things we learned

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.092
is that investigators are very interested

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.360
in Trump's state of mind.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.427
They had a lot of questions

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.096
about that specifically, Erin.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.364
They wanted to know

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:44.931
whether Trump

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.266
really believed some of the lies

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.001
that he was pushing in and around

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.636
January six. So notable.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.036
That's what

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.471
they're asking about right now.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.839
But also a sign, Erin, that

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.674
the January 6th investigation

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.309
is perhaps not as far along

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.044
as the classified documents probe.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:58.711
All right, Paul.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.647
And obviously, that is a big question

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.080
when these

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.782
when these come, if they come together

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.651
and those details could mean so much.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.885
Thank you very much.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.920
And of course, I should note, Elizabeth,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.788
Erin Griffin, as Paul is reporting.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.589
Speaking to prosecutors,

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.557
obviously choosing to do so

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.524
and do so forthrightly,

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.692
as she always does

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.460
in her role, as you see her here

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.362
so frequently as a contributor All right.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.198
OUTFRONT now, Stephanie Grisham, former

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.799
