00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.935
So they know at least by Monday.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:29.168
All right.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.303
So, John,

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.404
where do you think we are

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:34.407
in terms of an indictment or indictments

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.809
The special counsel is appointed

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.978
pursuant to certain regulations,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.681
and he is subject to the policies

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.315
and procedures

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.683
of the Department of Justice.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.550
And there

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.152
is something called the Justice Manual.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.021
It's a book every assisted U.S.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.122
attorney has it.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.089
And it says

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.424
if somebody is a target,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.893
you usually it flies their counsel

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.162
maybe you send them a target letter.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.164
And any good lawyers

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.232
when they receive that,

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.434
will ask for an opportunity for a meeting

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.102
and will present their arguments.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.405
Why the indictment should not be brought.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.606
And in this case, apparently,

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.308
they also have grievances,

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:08.908
what they claim

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.677
of prosecutorial misconduct. Right.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.078
And I think we can assume

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:12.712
that the Department

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:13.846
of the special counsel

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.515
has rejected those arguments.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.282
Now, remember,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.016
it still has to go

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.251
to the attorney general.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.018
It's ultimately

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.421
McCollum can approve a recommendation

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.523
or disapprove of it.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.591
But it seems like the grand jury,

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.261
particularly in Florida, is moving ahead.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.662
So it doesn't look like that

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.631
they're closing up shop and saying,

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.432
no, not today.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.833
It looks like they are All right.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.335
Well, I'll tell you what a target means.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.302
It means we believe

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.970
there is sufficient evidence

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.872
by which a jury could find you guilty

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.574
beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.542
Beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.810
Important to mention, the standard there.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:44.043
All right.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.011
So, Stephanie,

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.646
